  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "The anatomy layer: a segmental description of a heart. Every field has a CLOSED vocabulary so a spec can be validated, compared field-by-field against another spec, and used to state what is ABSENT — which a list of structure names cannot do.",
    "not_a_lesion_table": "There are deliberately no lesion entries here. This file defines the FIELDS and their ALLOWED VALUES — the taxonomy and nomenclature of the segmental approach (Van Praagh; Anderson). Individual hearts are described by filling these fields, and much of the filling is derivable from segmental notation by general rule (see utils/segmental.py).",
    "unknown": "Every field defaults to 'unknown'. Unknown is a real, useful state: it means the description is incomplete and must not be silently assumed. Assuming D-loop by default is what produced a D-looped cc-TGA.",
    "source": "TBD — textbook citation for the taxonomy itself, not per lesion"
  },

